Released in August 1967, the song reached number one on the US ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs|R&B]] [[record chart|chart]] and, in November, peaked on the ''Billboard'' [[Billboard Hot 100|Hot 100]] at No. 6.<ref>{{cite book |title= Top R&B/Hip-Hop Singles: 1942–2004|last=Whitburn |first=Joel |author-link=Joel Whitburn |year=2004 |publisher=[[Record Research]] |page=630}}</ref> Wilson's version also rose to number 11 and 15 upon the [[UK Singles Chart]] during 1969 and 1987 respectively.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.officialcharts.com/artist/5348/jackie-wilson/|title=Jackie Wilson|website=Official Charts.com}}</ref>

Brunswick Records then released an album titled ''Higher and Higher'' in November 1967. Its chart peak was No. 163 ([[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]]) and No. 28 (''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums|R&B Albums]] chart.)<ref name="rate_your_music" />{{deprecated source|certain=y|date=November 2024}}

The track was ranked No. 246 on ''[[Rolling Stone]]''{{'s}} list of [[The 500 Greatest Songs of All Time]], and was inducted into the [[Grammy Hall of Fame Award|Grammy Hall of Fame]] in 1999.

